# XCU yacc
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# yacc followed by c17 on the generated y.tab.c; each program supplies its
# own yylex, yyerror and main so the yacc library is not needed. Missing c17
# makes the test UNRESOLVED. Report formats are unspecified and never
# examined.

assertion  XCU.yacc.001
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#OUTPUT FILES
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       Without options yacc writes y.tab.c, not y.tab.h or y.output; the
           code file compiles, defines YYEOF as 0 and YYEMPTY as a negative
           number, and the parser evaluates input.
test       t/001-files-and-run.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.002
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Conflicts
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Declarations Section
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       Declared precedence and associativity resolve conflicts: higher
           precedence binds tighter, %left reduces, %right shifts, %nonassoc
           makes chained use a syntax error, and %prec gives a rule the
           precedence of a token.
test       t/002-precedence.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.003
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#OUTPUT FILES/Header File
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Interface to the Lexical Analyzer
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       -d writes y.tab.h with #define lines for the tokens; an explicit
           token number is used, other tokens are above 256 and distinct,
           and a %union gives YYSTYPE and yylval to the header.
test       t/003-header-and-tokens.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.004
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       -b pre names the outputs pre.tab.c, pre.tab.h and pre.output and
           no y.* files are written.
test       t/004-file-prefix.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.005
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       -v writes y.output, -l leaves #line out of the code file, and -t
           makes the debugging variable yydebug available with initial value
           zero.
test       t/005-options-v-l-t.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.006
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       -p xx renames yyparse, yylex and yyerror to xxparse, xxlex and
           xxerror; a program defining its own yyparse links with the
           generated code.
test       t/006-symbol-prefix.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.007
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Error Handling
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       A syntax error calls yyerror with "syntax error", the error token
           lets the parser recover, no second call is made while recovering,
           and yyerrok resets the recovery state.
test       t/007-error-recovery.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.008
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Error Handling
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       YYACCEPT makes yyparse return zero at once, YYABORT returns non-
           zero, and YYERROR returns non-zero without calling yyerror when
           there is no recovery rule.
test       t/008-accept-abort-error.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.009
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Grammar Rules in yacc
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Declarations Section
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       Semantic values flow through $$ and $n with union tags, the
           default value of a rule is its first element, a mid-rule action
           has a value, and %start overrides the first rule.
test       t/009-values.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.010
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Conflicts
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#STDERR
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       Conflicts are reported on standard error with a zero exit status;
           a shift/reduce conflict resolves to shift and a reduce/reduce
           conflict to the earlier rule.
test       t/010-conflict-defaults.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.011
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION/Interface to the Lexical Analyzer
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       A yylex that returns a negative value at end of input ends the
           parse successfully; end of input in the middle of a construct is
           a syntax error.
test       t/011-end-marker.sh

assertion  XCU.yacc.012
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/yacc.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD
since      1992
says       A missing grammar file, a missing operand and a non-terminal
           without a rule give a non-zero exit status.
test       t/012-errors.sh
